From 78e32fa93ff2a0233465837e929264f641f89f99 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 16:06:14 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat: daily practice streak on the Progress screen and the
 score screen

A day counts when at least one quiz was finished on it, by the device's local
time zone. PracticeStreak works the current run, the best run and today's state
out of the finish times of the saved quizzes, so nothing new is stored and the
database schema stays at version 1. The Progress screen gets a streak card, and
the score screen says whether the quiz started, kept or only repeated the day.

Saving a finished quiz now returns the earlier finish times from the same
transaction, so the outcome never depends on another save slipping in between.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01W1k2QnbmNmY8jdQT8nphjW
